You wouldn't have a newer version of the game then. When you're patching
and recompiling, you're replacing your complete installation of the game.

What you should do is: Examine all the patches you want to see if they're
all simultanously compatible with the same game version. If not, too bad.
Then download the source code of that game version and try to compile it
without patches. Watch for compiler errors. Once that works, apply the
patches one by one and watch out for error messages thrown by the 'patch'
program. Sometimes changing the order of the patches can help. When all
your patches are applied without patch errors, edit in the necessary
#defines and run the compilation again. When that succeeds, you have a
complete patched Slash'EM installation.

